# Astrodynamics

Course project for **Astrodynamics**, focused on applying orbital mechanics and numerical methods through Python.

## Course

**Astrodynamics**

The course covers the fundamentals of orbital mechanics, including the mathematical and computational methods used to model and analyze spacecraft trajectories.

## Project

The `SOL_Python` directory contains the Python tools developed for the course along the homeworks given during the semester.

```text
Projects/
├── SOL_Python/
│   ├── AstroConstants.py
│   ├── Graph_tools.py
│   ├── Math_tools.py
│   ├── Orbit_tools.py
│   └── Tracking_Obj.py
├── README.md
└── .gitignore
```

The project uses Python to implement and explore astrodynamics concepts through numerical calculations and simulations.



## Homeworks

# Week 1
Plot a SEZ on Quebec City and compute the differences between Geocentric and Geodesic.
- creation of Sol_Rotations.py plot a view of the earth.
- creation of geocVSgeod.py and related conversion methods.

# Week 2
Assess the AER of the Iss at a given epoch from Quebec City, and find its sub-satellite point.
- creation of Tracking_Obj.py defines Observer and Target class.
- creation of isspathing.py containing the actual computations for the homework.
- add some usefull Orbit and Math tools.

## Project status

Coursework in progress.